# Party banter in the Larders of Ill Omen and the dungeon. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible
# only while its condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections.

~ banter_soup
if flag.larders_cyrus_met and not flag.larders_cyrus_slain and not flag.larders_cyrus_hostile and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
interject name:thistle: Had the soup. Before he said who it was for. Good soup.
interject name:ratatoille: Barley and mutton. I tasted it first. Almost certainly mutton.
interject name:thistle: Almost?
endif
-> END

~ banter_cook
if flag.larders_cyrus_met and not flag.larders_cyrus_slain and not flag.larders_nadia_fate and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: He gives her extra bread so she won't be ready yet. That's kind. And it's horrible. I can't make it be just one.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Down here it's never just one. I'm praying for him as well, Godrick. Someone ought to.
endif
-> END

~ banter_chained
if flag.larders_nadia_met and not flag.larders_nadia_fate
interject tag:loyal: We're not leaving that girl in a cell. Whatever else we do down here.
interject tag:blunt: Then we'd better find her a way out that isn't through him.
endif
-> END

~ banter_escaped
if flag.larders_nadia_fate == "escaped" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:thistle
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Out in the scrap barrel! Clever girl. When she tells it in Vallaki, she'll leave the barrel out.
interject name:thistle: I won't. Best bit's the barrel.
endif
-> END

~ banter_shawl
if flag.larders_nadia_lost and name:kip_smudgewick and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:kip_smudgewick: We let her go up alone. I said it would be fine. I'm always saying it'll be fine.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: We all said it, Kip. Don't you go carrying it on your own.
endif
-> END

~ banter_brother
if flag.larders_anatol_fate == "unmasked" and not flag.larders_anatol_destroyed and name:thistle and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:thistle: Knew it. That priest smelled wrong from the door.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He wore the dawn like a coat, to lure decent people close. I find I am very angry, and I don't mind it at all.
interject tag:blunt: Then let's go back and give him some.
endif
-> END

~ banter_doru
if flag.larders_doru_fate == "rest" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Father Donavich will want to know his son is at rest. He should hear it from a priest. I'll tell him myself, gently.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'll come with you. I'm good at standing quiet in doorways.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bones
if flag.larders_hall_told and not flag.larders_furnace_quenched and name:ratatoille and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:ratatoille: A lamp fed by a furnace fed by nothing. A machine for keeping one room lit forever. As craft, I almost admire it.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Rat. There's a table made of bones under that lamp. Admire it quieter.
endif
-> END

~ banter_dark
if flag.larders_furnace_quenched and name:wren_featherfoot and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Every green lamp under the castle, out at once. Somewhere upstairs, somebody just put his glass down.
interject tag:cheerful: Good. Let him wonder about something for once.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Will he send someone down to look? I'd like to be somewhere else when they look.
endif
-> END

~ banter_niche
if flag.larders_niche_opened and name:kip_smudgewick and name:ratatoille
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Sold the wrong man vinegar and got bricked up with his stock. That's every merchant's nightmare. I've had that exact dream.
interject name:ratatoille: To be fair, vinegar sold as wine is a crime. Not a bricking-up crime. A strongly worded letter.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Rat!
endif
-> END
